  nonce: 763f  # 763f
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT (as re-titled 2026-09-25 to the modelling question).\n\n- Emission site: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/bash.py:1005-1030 -- each declaration_command with an `export` child mints Symbol(kind=\"export\") with id make_symbol_id(..., start_line, ..., var_name, \"export\"); no per-file dedup. bash.py commits since the 09-25 review: f562635f72 (docstrings), eea92d5a22 (WI-fisoh payload) -- neither touches this.\n- Repro (scratch a.sh, `hypergumbo survey . --out`): `export CI_TIMEOUT=1` (L2), `export CI_TIMEOUT=2` (L4) -> bash:a.sh:2-2:CI_TIMEOUT:export sha256:00e9cbe08614e456 and bash:a.sh:4-4:CI_TIMEOUT:export sha256:b85aedac5c16f4a6 -- identical to the 09-25 review: same (path,name,kind), distinct stable_ids. INV-bazij still satisfied.\n- ADJACENT, SAME SITE, relevant to the decision: the code takes only the FIRST variable_assignment child (find_child_by_type), so\n    `export A=1 B=2` -> only A emitted, B dropped;\n    bare `export CI_TIMEOUT` -> no node;\n    `declare -x D=1` -> no node (declare -x also exports); `readonly R=1` -> no node.\n  Whichever model is chosen (one per statement vs one per variable) these four shapes need the same answer; I found no open row for them (grep of open items for bash).\n- Not re-measured: the body's SCRIPTS-substrate 7.0% / FORGEJO_TOKEN 5x figures (they are pre-v6 stable_id numbers; the INV-bazij framing they supported is retired per the 09-25 entries).\n\nProposed: add the multi-name / bare / declare -x shapes to the description (or file them as a sibling) so the modelling decision covers them; priority question from 09-25 still open with the owner."  # 763f
