    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md`, Family C), finding F24.6, previously folded onto WI-bupim. Full original evidence remains on WI-bupim's pass-24 discussion entry (2026-06-02T04:54:12).\n\n## The question\n\nThe bash analyzer treats each `export VAR_NAME=...` statement as a distinct Symbol node (packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/bash.py ~L1005-1030: every declaration_command with an `export` child mints Symbol(kind=\"export\") with no per-file dedup). A variable exported several times in one file therefore has several nodes sharing (path, name, kind). Decide the model: is each `export` statement a declaration (one symbol per statement), or is the variable one symbol with several assignments?\n\nRepro (dev 134a06d505, `hypergumbo survey`): a.sh with `export CI_TIMEOUT=1` (L2) and `export CI_TIMEOUT=2` (L4) emits bash:a.sh:2-2:CI_TIMEOUT:export and bash:a.sh:4-4:CI_TIMEOUT:export. At filing, `scripts/auto-pr` declared `CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` 3 times and `FORGEJO_TOKEN` appeared 5x (not re-measured).\n\nThis is a MODELLING choice, not an identity collision: the duplicate nodes carry DISTINCT stable_ids (sha256:00e9cbe08614e456 vs sha256:b85aedac5c16f4a6 in the repro), and INV-bazij (stable_id mass collisions) has been satisfied since 06-09. The original P2 rationale was that INV-bazij breach.\n\n## Options\n\n**(a) One symbol per variable.** When `export VAR_NAME` is seen and a Symbol with the same (path, name, kind) exists in the file, do not emit another (optionally record the extra sites on it). Matches the \"one Symbol per concept\" framing; the redundant nodes carry no extra semantics (same name, same shell scope, same export semantics).\n\n**(b) One symbol per declaration statement.** Keep today's behaviour and document it; each node keeps its own declaration site.\n\nRecommendation at filing: (a).\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Sibling sharing this modelling decision: **WI-luzit-zujag-banid-valot-dofuk-jumom-korih-zazil** -- the same emission site reads only the FIRST variable_assignment, so `export A=1 B=2` drops B, and bare `export X`, `declare -x D=1` and `readonly R=1` emit no symbol. Whichever model is chosen here must give those shapes the same answer.\n- Parent: **INV-bazij** (satisfied). Siblings under it: WI-bupim (typed-tier name disambiguation), WI-sirid (markdown within-file duplicate headings), WI-typescript-hash-input-insufficient (TS cross-name collapse). Cousin: WI-vodin (canonical id-format static check).\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 00e9
